{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e","id":1398392,"title":"Is Usurpation the right term still in 3e?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-23T11:41:47-07:00","id":1398392,"title":"Is Usurpation the right term still in 3e?","content":"Disclaimer: This is designed to promote a discussion and any assertions made are just my opinion not objective reality.<br /> <br /> One of the more interesting (to me) lore bits that was dropped by the devs have been changes in presentation of the First Age. In particular, the idea that there was not a unified state as depicted in previous editions.<br /> <br /> In particular it is no longer the Solar Deliberative (which was ruled by solars through what amounted to Divine Right over all of Creation) but instead the Second Deliberative (where Solars has outsized influence but no longer ruled through divine right).<br /> <br /> The other bit is that even the Second Deliberative did not rule over creation as a unified state (central, federal, or even a confederate model of governance). This implies that there was significant land either ungoverned by the second deliberative or rival polities.<br /> <br /> <br /> This leads to an interesting question: is the term \u201cthe Usurpation\u201d even still the right term? A portion (To me) of the previous thematics in Exalted had been that there was a cyclic nature to Creation\u2019s history, with the rulers of each age finding their rule usurped as they grew abusive or corrupt with their power. In previous editions, the term usurpation (which has the implication of actively taking power from the previous regime illegitimately, but retaining a semblance of the status quo regime) followed the form and function of the events that had transpired.<br /> <br /> My question is: is the term Usurpation still the right term for what transpired? Revolution would work (as the Second Deliberative was replaced with a new status quo). It feels like Usurpation is an artifact (heh) of a bygone era that that no longer fits with the history of Creation as presented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T11:58:31-07:00","id":1398395,"title":"","content":"Honestly even in previous editions Usurpation feels like a biased term to use. It's always an appropriate way to describe how Solars and Lunars would see the event, but I feel Sidereals and DBs wouldn't look back on those events in such a negative light.<br /> <br /> History is written by the victors, so what kind of victor calls their own rise to power &quot;THE TERRIBLE BETRAYAL&quot;?<br /> <br /> <i>The Righting of Fate</i><br /> <br /> <i>The Dragon's Landing</i><br /> <br /> <i>The Castigation of Sun and Moon</i><br /> <br /> <i>The Second Revolution</i><br /> <br /> Anything would sound better than &quot;The Usurpation&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T12:03:43-07:00","id":1398399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398395#post1398395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly even in previous editions Usurpation feels like a biased term to use. It's always an appropriate way to describe how Solars and Lunars would see the event, but I feel Sidereals and DBs wouldn't look back on those events in such a negative light.<br /> <br /> History is written by the victors, so what kind of victor calls their own rise to power &amp;quot;THE TERRIBLE BETRAYAL&amp;quot;?<br /> <br /> <i>The Righting of Fate</i><br /> <br /> <i>The Dragon's Landing</i><br /> <br /> <i>The Castigation of Sun and Moon</i><br /> <br /> <i>The Second Revolution</i><br /> <br /> Anything would sound better than &amp;quot;The Usurpation&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Absolutely: the Lunars especially I could see defining it that way, but even then, the fact that Creation was not ruled wholly be the Second Deliberative and that the celestial exalts (solars especially) did not rule through what amounts to be Divine Right does seem to change the context imo even further away from a use of Usurpation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T12:37:38-07:00","id":1398407,"title":"","content":"It has never made sense in any edition for Realm scholars to call it &quot;the Usurpation.&quot; It's most likely described as &quot;the fall of the Anathema,&quot; &quot;the purge of the Anathema,&quot; or the like; we certainly see such naming in such material as the 1e Aspect books.<br /> <br /> Despite the changes in 3e, it's still reasonable to speak of it as an usurpation. The Dragon-Blooded may have had more of a role in the Second Deliberative than in its 1e/2e equivalents, but the end result was the same: With the Solars dead, the Lunars driven out, and the Sidereals withdrawn to Heaven, power that once resided in other hands was consolidated \u2014 indeed, usurped \u2014 by the Dragon-Blooded alone. And if the term is used primarily by the Exalted whose power was taken in this way? From their perspective, their power was usurped.<br /> <br /> (There is ultimately a certain amount of legacy text here that might have been changed if the core book developers had been so inclined! But the fact that certain things <i>could</i> have been changed does not mean that keeping them the same was necessarily wrong.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T12:51:09-07:00","id":1398410,"title":"","content":"Historical &quot;accuracy&quot; aside, I think it's still a useful term for informing player expectations. It makes sense for a player wanting to play a Solar to be told the corrupt rulers of the world actually usurped their rule and how the PC's return might herald a glorious golden age.<br /> <br /> Certainly it would be deflating to read the Solar splatbook and be told of how the heroic DBs and Sidereals stopped your nefarious schemes and how despite your best intentions your return heralds nothing but trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T13:02:11-07:00","id":1398416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398407#post1398407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has never made sense in any edition for Realm scholars to call it &amp;quot;the Usurpation.&amp;quot; It's most likely described as &amp;quot;the fall of the Anathema,&amp;quot; &amp;quot;the purge of the Anathema,&amp;quot; or the like; we certainly see such naming in such material as the 1e Aspect books.<br /> <br /> Despite the changes in 3e, it's still reasonable to speak of it as an usurpation. The Dragon-Blooded may have had more of a role in the Second Deliberative than in its 1e/2e equivalents, but the end result was the same: With the Solars dead, the Lunars driven out, and the Sidereals withdrawn to Heaven, power that once resided in other hands was consolidated \u2014 indeed, usurped \u2014 by the Dragon-Blooded alone. And if the term is used primarily by the Exalted whose power was taken in this way? From their perspective, their power was usurped.<br /> <br /> (There is ultimately a certain amount of legacy text here that might have been changed if the core book developers had been so inclined! But the fact that certain things <i>could</i> have been changed does not mean that keeping them the same was necessarily wrong.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting! But it does raise some questions about the Second Deliberative. All of Creation was not under their control, how much wasn\u2019t? Was it substantive enough for it there to have been settlers who sought away from the from the Deliberative? Did they create competing states? Was the threat posed by the Solars such that the powers that led the Usurpation sought foreign intervention?<br /> <br /> Sorry for all the follow-on questions. It\u2019s just an interesting thing to discuss for me because creates implications about the setting thematics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T13:37:56-07:00","id":1398424,"title":"","content":"I like it because I can have a character repeatedly refer to the 'ursapation' and have people thinking the NPC is just saying usurpation wrong, he leads you home and plot-twist... intelligent bears have taken over and made humans second class citizens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T14:16:58-07:00","id":1398431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398424#post1398424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it because I can have a character repeatedly refer to the 'ursapation' and have people thinking the NPC is just saying usurpation wrong, he leads you home and plot-twist... intelligent bears have taken over and made humans second class citizens.</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of a story teller would ever do such a thing?<br /> <br /> *smirk*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T14:30:42-07:00","id":1398438,"title":"","content":"Basically it\u2019s how the Solars (and I guess the Lunars) refer to it. The way Southerners in the 1950s used to call the Civil War the War Between the States.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T16:53:37-07:00","id":1398464,"title":"","content":"It's punchy, memorable and it gets the key points across.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T20:08:47-07:00","id":1398512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398438#post1398438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically it\u2019s how the Solars (and I guess the Lunars) refer to it. The way Southerners in the 1950s used to call the Civil War the War Between the States.</div> </div> </div> </div>You <b>did not</b> just make an equivalency between Southern racists and Solars and Lunars in your statement there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T20:59:47-07:00","id":1398522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398438#post1398438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically it\u2019s how the Solars (and I guess the Lunars) refer to it. The way Southerners in the 1950s used to call the Civil War the War Between the States.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is a tasteless comment right now. Consider yourself chided.</span><br /> <br /> Also, Solars call it the Usurpation because it was a bunch of vassals rising up against their lords. It's literally true in feudal terms rather than a moral judgement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398512#post1398512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You <b>did not</b> just make an equivalency between Southern racists and Solars and Lunars in your statement there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The timing is horribly off.<br /> <br /> The slave owning deranged psychopath demigods were replaced by slave owning psychopath quasi-deities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-24-2020, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T21:18:53-07:00","id":1398525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398512#post1398512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You <b>did not</b> just make an equivalency between Southern racists and Solars and Lunars in your statement there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the point was not to compare the morality of the 2 groups, but simply to give an example of how the losers of a conflict might remember the conflict differently from what the victors wrote into the history books.<br /> <br /> Edit: Welp, that's what I get for taking forever to post, the discussion got moderated in the meantime. Apologies if my own post offends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 06-24-2020, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T00:28:58-07:00","id":1398541,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I\u2019m sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T01:18:36-07:00","id":1398543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398416#post1398416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting! But it does raise some questions about the Second Deliberative. All of Creation was not under their control, how much wasn\u2019t? Was it substantive enough for it there to have been settlers who sought away from the from the Deliberative? Did they create competing states? Was the threat posed by the Solars such that the powers that led the Usurpation sought foreign intervention?<br /> <br /> Sorry for all the follow-on questions. It\u2019s just an interesting thing to discuss for me because creates implications about the setting thematics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your questions but I truly believe that they are not supposed to have one definitive answer. There was a long discussion on another topic about this and I think I'm not the only one who argued the pages are left semi blank on purpose to let each player invent whatever stories that would contextualize The Usurpation.<br /> <br /> To answer your question on a more personal level, though : I tend to see The First Age as a very vast world, vast enough that someone that doesn't want to have problem with neighboring Solars and Lunars kingdoms could try and go far away build a kingdom for himself. But at the same time, I think the First Age was chaotic and warfare-y enough that many Solars/Lunars/DB would one day find these isolated kingdoms and would rain hell upon them (The Great Curse being a huge motor of this dynamic, think of a Solar going &quot;My great-ancestor was wronged by this guy who fled with his armies, now the time has come to show that MY JUSTICE IS LIMITED BY NEITHER TIME NOR SPACE NOR BLOODLINE&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T01:19:01-07:00","id":1398544,"title":"","content":"It's not a terrible comparison in other times as, again, the First Age Solars were a bunch of Nero and Caligula types who were given the power of the Olympians and lorded over billions of helpless mortals.<br /> <br /> (It's a <b>dramatic irony</b> that the Solars remember it as being overthrown by the EVIL Dragonblooded [and Sidereals] when they really had it coming--and now the roles are reversed with the Dragonblooded the corrupt tyrants)<br /> <br /> It's just, right now, very bad timing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T01:41:40-07:00","id":1398547,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I get it. I can be clueless about stuff like that sometimes.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think the irony could make for some really good role playing.<br /> <br /> Question though<br /> <br /> Did the Gold Faction exist at the time of the uprising? If they did, why didn\u2019t they try and prevent it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T01:44:18-07:00","id":1398548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398544#post1398544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a terrible comparison in other times as, again, the First Age Solars were a bunch of Nero and Caligula types who were given the power of the Olympians and lorded over billions of helpless mortals.<br /> <br /> (It's a <b>dramatic irony</b> that the Solars remember it as being overthrown by the EVIL Dragonblooded [and Sidereals] when they really had it coming--and now the roles are reversed with the Dragonblooded the corrupt tyrants)<br /> <br /> It's just, right now, very bad timing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do gather from the material, for the record, that this simplified rendition is not the approach that Ex3 is taking. (For example there are multiple references in many books of Dragonblooded headed Kingdoms even in the First Age, which puts the so-called slave owning nature of the Solar deliberative in question)<br /> <br /> Everything has nuance and no one group is automatically the \u201cCaligulas and Neros\u201d, any more than the current Realm can be wholly compared to unsavoury authoritarian/slave owning regimes of recent memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 06-24-2020, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T01:53:34-07:00","id":1398550,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8959_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8959\" data-vbnamecard=\"8959\">prototype00</a> yes, but the First Age Solars were literally insane (power-mad) because of the Great Curse. Or is that no longer accurate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T01:54:11-07:00","id":1398551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398548#post1398548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do gather from the material, for the record, that this simplified rendition is not the approach that Ex3 is taking.<br /> <br /> Everything has nuance and no one group is automatically the \u201cCaligulas and Neros\u201d, any more than the current Realm can be wholly compared to unsavoury authoritarian/slave owning regimes of recent memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Evil is a matter of perspective in Bronze Age society. Things are a bit different but there are still going to be a lot of argument either way for both overthrowing the Solars and overthrowing the Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> I remember on RPG.net, a Dragonblooded fan talked about how he envisioned the Dragonblooded as individuals who were cruel and dictatorial to their subjects but whenever they would be attacked by Fae or whatnot that they would fight to the death to defend them.<br /> <br /> A developer then came onto the thread and said, &quot;No, actually, the majority of Dragonblooded would probably go 'fuck those guys.' Only a rare few would actually find the lives of a bunch of peasants worth risking their own.&quot;<br /> <br /> But some WOULD and that skews the whole business. Ditto the Usurption. All of the Solars were insane but some were insane in ways that wouldn't have necessarily been horrifying. They also could have been helped but it was RISKIER.<br /> <br /> That's just my take on it, though. 3rd Edition has its own very different view, though, and I am loving what I'm seeing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T01:54:39-07:00","id":1398552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398547#post1398547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question though<br /> <br /> Did the Gold Faction exist at the time of the uprising? If they did, why didn\u2019t they try and prevent it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wondered this one as well and my hypothesis was that the Gold Faction didn't exist in an established fashion as they could be today. I also think it's possible their most prominent member at the time were &quot;taken care off&quot; by the Bronze Faction firsthand, when they started plotting and realized some Sidereals did not believe getting rid of Solars and Lunars was a good idea.<br /> <br /> I don't know enough about Sidereals, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T02:00:45-07:00","id":1398555,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24291\" data-vbnamecard=\"24291\">Chausse</a> thanks. That makes a lot of sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T02:03:38-07:00","id":1398558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398551#post1398551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Evil is a matter of perspective in Bronze Age society. Things are a bit different but there are still going to be a lot of argument either way for both overthrowing the Solars and overthrowing the Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> I remember on RPG.net, a Dragonblooded fan talked about how he envisioned the Dragonblooded as individuals who were cruel and dictatorial to their subjects but whenever they would be attacked by Fae or whatnot that they would fight to the death to defend them.<br /> <br /> A developer then came onto the thread and said, &amp;quot;No, actually, the majority of Dragonblooded would probably go 'fuck those guys.' Only a rare few would actually find the lives of a bunch of peasants worth risking their own.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> But some WOULD and that skews the whole business. Ditto the Usurption. All of the Solars were insane but some were insane in ways that wouldn't have necessarily been horrifying. They also could have been helped but it was RISKIER.<br /> <br /> That's just my take on it, though. 3rd Edition has its own very different view, though, and I am loving what I'm seeing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I guess not all of the insane Solars were evil.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not that familiar with 3e. Could one of you guys summarize 3e\u2019s view of the Usurpation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T02:04:09-07:00","id":1398559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398550#post1398550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8959_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8959\" data-vbnamecard=\"8959\">prototype00</a> yes, but the First Age Solars were literally insane (power-mad) because of the Great Curse. Or is that no longer accurate?</div> </div> </div> </div>We don\u2019t know. The Great Curse seems to be more subtle these days, and while awful, doesn\u2019t go full on baby eating evil (for reference, check out Elder Lunars, even Raksi the trope namer isn\u2019t pants on head insane anymore).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T02:07:30-07:00","id":1398560,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8959_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8959\" data-vbnamecard=\"8959\">prototype00</a> awesome \ud83d\ude0a. I haven\u2019t had a chance to read Fangs at the Gate yet, but I\u2019m defo looking forward to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T02:21:46-07:00","id":1398564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398560#post1398560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> awesome \ud83d\ude0a. I haven\u2019t had a chance to read Fangs at the Gate yet, but I\u2019m defo looking forward to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, if you haven\u2019t read Fangs yet my apologies, it\u2019s the first look we have had at Exalted that have had all the ravages of millennia of the Great Curse heaped on them, and without that I shouldn\u2019t expect you to know about the hints of the setting we were given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T02:51:45-07:00","id":1398568,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8959_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8959\" data-vbnamecard=\"8959\">prototype00</a> thanks. I\u2019d love to discuss some of the setting stuff after I\u2019ve had a chance to read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T03:07:50-07:00","id":1398570,"title":"","content":"It was the Usurpation that created the Gold and Bronze Faction; but the Gold were subourned, isolated, or killed. Centuries later, the reincarnation of their leader refounded the gold faction, but with hardly any Solars around it was a tiny group who did little beyond saying &quot;I told you so&quot;. Then, suddenly 5 years ago the Gold Faction actually became viable again, and a number of Sidereals recently joined. It's still very much a minority though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T03:08:20-07:00","id":1398572,"title":"","content":"Assuming 3rd ed Sidereals doesn't change this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T04:09:20-07:00","id":1398578,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine that there was a growing faction of sidereals who had misgivings about the whole thing and were turning off the idea of constantly hunting down the lunars and solars but the status quo meant there was very little they could do about it and they just had to keep quiet.<br /> <br /> Then the solars came back, and these sidereals saw that the winds were turning. <br /> <br /> It's probably the younger ones, mostly. They never saw the first age so all they have to go off is stories from the elders about insane god kings and the current elder lunars, who are actually not that bad, all things considered. So they're like &quot;hey, you know, maybe they're exaggerating. Maybe they weren't as unsalvageable as they thought. We have fresh solars now who will listen to us. We can nip the problem at the bud peacefully&quot;<br /> <br /> And there might be others who go &quot;Yeah, if we keep the wyld hunts up now the solars are gonna figure out whose behind them and join in with the lunars trying to murder us. We get enough faces eaten as is.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T04:46:41-07:00","id":1398581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398572#post1398572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming 3rd ed Sidereals doesn't change this.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I also think there are a few elements in the core book and Fangs at the Gate that could be developed into a point that Sidereals on the whole have had more pressing things to worry about than the Solars, and the dichotomy amounted to those who were actively involved in promoting the Realm and opposing the Lunars and those who were not.<br /> <br /> In addition to that, I'm attached to an idea that the backstory was one in which the matter was important enough that the Fivescore Fellowship was in agreement to act as one when a majority position was reached.<br /> <br /> I'm kind of hoping for some significant revisions to the prophecy as a whole; I've grown disillusioned with a presentation in which the options for the Sidereals were given to them by prophecy rather than their own debate about what to do in response to it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T07:21:29-07:00","id":1398598,"title":"","content":"I, also, would prefer if the Sidereals portended doom (prompting the Usurpation), but the Visions of Gold and Bronze were not, themselves, prophecy (but rather plans formulated by the Sidereals).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T07:34:47-07:00","id":1398599,"title":"","content":"The Sidereals are a group of people who are very bureaucratic and know-it-alls who work behind the scenes. They're essentially a race of academics merged with the Illuminati. Most of them were probably okay with the Usurpation at the beginning but the simple fact is that it has been one big shit sandwich nearly constantly afterward.<br /> <br /> 3rd Edition's primary focus seems to be dialing down the anime mecha influence and dialing up the more Conan the Barbarian/Hyborian Age/wuxia/Crouching Tiger influences. However, it's still keeping most of the fundamentals intact even if the Sun is now a ball of gas and not an enormous mech piloted to fight a corrupted Autocthonia.<br /> <br /> I mean:<br /> <br /> * The fairies still ate 95% of creation<br /> * Technology has gone from rail cars and flying machines to quasi-Medieval<br /> * Even if the Solars are a huge danger, and they are, you need to have Solars fighting the corrupted Solars of the Abyssals and Infernals. Because the Abyssals may have a POINT that it'd be better to recreate Creation in the Underworld as a paradise--but it's a point most people would find to be lunacy.<br /> * The Scarlet Empress did a pretty neat job but she's gone now and a lot of her success was stealing a Solar weapon to begin with.<br /> <br /> The Gold Faction also isn't the FRIENDS of the Solars.<br /> <br /> They're people who want to USE the Solars.<br /> <br /> The Solars can win them over with Epic Charisma because that's what Solars do but most are coming very much into it like the Aes Sedai and Rand Al'Thor.<br /> <br /> &quot;We need him to kill Satan but he's otherwise a ticking time bomb.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-24-2020, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T08:56:51-07:00","id":1398607,"title":"","content":"That's certainly... a take.<br /> <br /> 2E presents the Visions of Gold, Bronze and Darkness a little too starkly for my taste. But the 2E presentation had Sidereals who were against the idea from the beginning. They were the first casualties of the Usurpation, and involved CK murdering his best friend in cold blood (which might be why the Sids call it the Usurpation). And this gels, somewhat, with what you wrote: the majority went along with it. But 2E also showed us 1st Age Solars stringing mutilated humans together so their screams could be played as an instrument and saw them breeding slave races. So I hardly see the default Sidereal looking at Creation as a dispassionate academic or a plotting Illuminati. They're people, watching the people they love abused.<br /> <br /> The Fair Folk didn't &quot;eat 95%&quot; of Creation though.<br /> I wouldn't characterize the technology as medieval.<br /> I strongly don't feel that one &quot;needs&quot; to fight Abyssals (or Infernals) with Solars.<br /> Autochothon and the Exalted built the Sword of Creation -- Twilight Savants may have had the biggest single influence as a collective class, but I dispute the Sword being labelled a &quot;Solar&quot; weapon in the 3E paradigm (and you can't steal something that isn't owned -- if no-one owns the superweapon that will save all life from extinction, you have every right to homestead it).<br /> <br /> And I don't think it's particularly helpful to characterise the Gold Faction as wanting to &quot;use&quot; the Solars. Certainly there are Sidereals who want to use the Solars. And you're making a wider point here, I get that, but I think you've oversimplified past the point of helpfulness. Especially if you're trying to run a mixed game.<br /> <br /> Looping back to OP, the Dragon-Blooded don't call it the Usurpation. I think every other faction has a good enough reason to see it as such, whether the Deebs are literally throwing down the holders of the Creation Ruling Mandate, or just betraying the other Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T12:30:53-07:00","id":1398634,"title":"","content":"My gathering is any folks who favored the Vision of Gold who weren't in the Usurpation project just sat out. A big thing that I think the devs want to give Sidereals is a bit of an actual Fellowship feel and this idea that they do have generally a professional working, institutional relationship. Thew ay the Visions were presented were pretty mutually exclusive. Bronze menat going all in with Usuraption. Gold meant going all-in with reforming the Solars. If <i>either</i> failed they'd get Darkness. The majority of Sidereals decided on Bronze. The ones who disagreed probably were just reasonable enough to know that if they interered they'd fuck everything up and get everyone killed or things ruined.<br /> <br /> That's kind of how I see it basically. A lot of Lunars probably consider those Sidereals just as guilty for the Usurpation as the active ones like Chejob since willing inaction is a form of support in itself. The Gold as it exists today is an entirely new organizaiton that draws its name from that old Prophecy one but probably has as much related to it as however many Immortals units existed in the history of the world have had with one-another.<br /> <br /> It also to me also adds a layer of &quot;professional detachment&quot; Sidereals can get into that's kind of weirdly unique to them and also results in interesting on-the-ground conflict probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T15:10:41-07:00","id":1398649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I hardly see the default Sidereal looking at Creation as a dispassionate academic or a plotting Illuminati. They're people, watching the people they love abused </div> </div> </div>They're also people who live completely apart from Creation in Heaven.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Fair Folk didn't &quot;eat 95%&quot; of Creation though. </div> </div> </div>The vast vast majority of Creation no longer exists and has been unmade by the Children of the Wyld so that seems splitting hairs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I strongly don't feel that one &quot;needs&quot; to fight Abyssals (or Infernals) with Solars. </div> </div> </div>I'm open to suggestions for who you think can beat the godlike beings about to destroy reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I don't think it's particularly helpful to characterise the Gold Faction as wanting to &quot;use&quot; the Solars. Certainly there are Sidereals who want to use the Solars. And you're making a wider point here, I get that, but I think you've oversimplified past the point of helpfulness. Especially if you're trying to run a mixed game. </div> </div> </div>The Cult of the Illuminated is 100% a scam to control Solars from behind the scenes and it's the Gold Faction's big tent project.<br /> <br /> but in a mixed game, it's almost always &quot;You're the exception to the rule.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-24-2020, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T17:30:06-07:00","id":1398667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398649#post1398649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Cult of the Illuminated is 100% a scam to control Solars from behind the scenes and it's the Gold Faction's big tent project.</div> </div> </div> </div>The presentation is less cynical in Ex3, where the cult was not inspired by gold faction, though they do channel young Solars towards it for protection and guidance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T17:36:48-07:00","id":1398669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398599#post1398599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> * The fairies still ate 95% of creation<br /> * Technology has gone from rail cars and flying machines to quasi-Medieval<br /> * Even if the Solars are a huge danger, and they are, you need to have Solars fighting the corrupted Solars of the Abyssals and Infernals. Because the Abyssals may have a POINT that it'd be better to recreate Creation in the Underworld as a paradise--but it's a point most people would find to be lunacy.<br /> * The Scarlet Empress did a pretty neat job but she's gone now and a lot of her success was stealing a Solar weapon to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of these points is unlike the others in that it is a very subjective opinion of either the facts as they stand in the setting or the manner in which things will ultimately be written, if not both.<br /> <br /> Like, why are Abyssals and Infernals any more difficult for Dragon Blooded, Sidereals and Lunars to fight than Solars have been throughout the entirety of the Second Age?<br /> <br /> Wyld Hunts have killed Solars, what makes the other two so much more dangerous?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T17:46:21-07:00","id":1398672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398669#post1398669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of these points is unlike the others in that it is a very subjective opinion of either the facts as they stand in the setting or the manner in which things will ultimately be written, if not both.<br /> <br /> Like, why are Abyssals and Infernals any more difficult for Dragon Blooded, Sidereals and Lunars to fight than Solars have been throughout the entirety of the Second Age?<br /> <br /> Wyld Hunts have killed Solars, what makes the other two so much more dangerous?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyld Hunts have killed Solars who have been alone, lost, bereft of allies, and disadvantaged by having no idea what they were. The Abyssals and Infernals have armies, Primordial Patrons, and the ghosts of First Age soldiers at their back plus Akuma. The Scarlet Empress was also in power and the Dragonblooded Empire was united rather than a shattered civil-war torn shadow of its former self.<br /> <br /> Obviously, you can run your campaign any way you want to do so. You may not want to focus on the existential threat that the Abyssals and Infernals pose. There's even an argument that you don't have to because they'll be fighting each other.<br /> <br /> However, from my mostly objective 3rd person omniscient perspective, if the Solars don't fight them then the Abyssals and Infernals will win. Creation will end and the other factions will not be able to beat them. Part of this may be Solar bias but Exalted is a game that has them at the heart.<br /> <br /> The only exception to &quot;The Solars are needed to save Creation&quot; is if the PCs build Alchemicals, Lunars, or Dragonblooded who save Creation instead. PCs have their own magic that warps the setting. Otherwise, it's all on the Unconquered Sun's children.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398667#post1398667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The presentation is less cynical in Ex3, where the cult was not inspired by gold faction, though they do channel young Solars towards it for protection and guidance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I don't approve of that change completely. Mostly because part of the fun is that the Solars are such charismatic badasses that even if it starts as a scam, it will rapidly fall in line.<br /> <br /> But I'm sure plenty of awesome adventures will come from the change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-24-2020, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T18:40:51-07:00","id":1398679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398672#post1398672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wyld Hunts have killed Solars who have been alone, lost, bereft of allies, and disadvantaged by having no idea what they were. The Abyssals and Infernals have armies, Primordial Patrons, and the ghosts of First Age soldiers at their back plus Akuma. The Scarlet Empress was also in power and the Dragonblooded Empire was united rather than a shattered civil-war torn shadow of its former self.<br /> <br /> Obviously, you can run your campaign any way you want to do so. You may not want to focus on the existential threat that the Abyssals and Infernals pose. There's even an argument that you don't have to because they'll be fighting each other.<br /> <br /> However, from my mostly objective 3rd person omniscient perspective, if the Solars don't fight them then the Abyssals and Infernals will win. Creation will end and the other factions will not be able to beat them. Part of this may be Solar bias but Exalted is a game that has them at the heart.<br /> <br /> The only exception to &quot;The Solars are needed to save Creation&quot; is if the PCs build Alchemicals, Lunars, or Dragonblooded who save Creation instead. PCs have their own magic that warps the setting. Otherwise, it's all on the Unconquered Sun's children.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ah, I don't approve of that change completely. Mostly because part of the fun is that the Solars are such charismatic badasses that even if it starts as a scam, it will rapidly fall in line.<br /> <br /> But I'm sure plenty of awesome adventures will come from the change.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a very... old-fashioned attitude.<br /> <br /> I don't think the idea of Abyssals and Infernals was accurate even to prior Editions, at least not comprehensively. Right now? Some of them have some of those things. Others operate in different fashion.<br /> <br /> Besides, if a Wyld Hunt (preferably with Sidereals, assuming they don't act independently) needs to adapt to opponents with armies, there are ways to do that. Fighting the army in the field is the bad way. Sneaking through the army while it has made camp to get at the commanding Exalt in their tent and try to strike hard and fast carries better prospects.<br /> <br /> An old fashioned attitude would actually afford the Solar or Abyssal less than Supernal or Chtonic Ability would provide, but even assuming that it can be fair to not presume every such Exalt is rocking Essence 5 Charms.<br /> <br /> That is for the martial ones. A Midnight Caste might be assumed to be a bit more dangerous than a Zenith, but insurmountably so?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T23:31:23-07:00","id":1398720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398649#post1398649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're also people who live completely apart from Creation in Heaven.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The vast vast majority of Creation no longer exists and has been unmade by the Children of the Wyld so that seems splitting hairs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm open to suggestions for who you think can beat the godlike beings about to destroy reality.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Cult of the Illuminated is 100% a scam to control Solars from behind the scenes and it's the Gold Faction's big tent project.<br /> <br /> but in a mixed game, it's almost always &amp;quot;You're the exception to the rule.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>CT, you are running a lot of assumptions that, frankly, aren't true in 3E. Most of them weren't even true in 2E outside of memes.<br /> <br /> I have no idea how to engage with this productively, so I'm going to bow out of the conversation here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T23:37:39-07:00","id":1398721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398720#post1398720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> CT, you are running a lot of assumptions that, frankly, aren't true in 3E. Most of them weren't even true in 2E outside of memes.<br /> <br /> I have no idea how to engage with this productively, so I'm going to bow out of the conversation here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okkkkkay.<br /> <br /> Sorry to hear that. It would have been nice to hear your thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T00:19:37-07:00","id":1398725,"title":"","content":"I could always give my take.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398649#post1398649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're also people who live completely apart from Creation in Heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even in 1e and 2e, Sidereals have access to the Acquaintances Merit representing their developing meaningful connections to people outside of Yu-Shan. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398649#post1398649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The vast vast majority of Creation no longer exists and has been unmade by the Children of the Wyld so that seems splitting hairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that the borders of Creation were also greatly expanded in the First Age. And even a single Exalt can - with heroic effort and some esoteric tricks, mind - win back a little of the map from the Wyld. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398649#post1398649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm open to suggestions for who you think can beat the godlike beings about to destroy reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>3E has moved away from the model where numerous all-powerful beings are poised to bring about the destruction of reality, as well as the notion that the Exalted would be insufficient to handle it if they were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-25-2020, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T08:24:42-07:00","id":1398787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3E has moved away from the model where numerous all-powerful beings are poised to bring about the destruction of reality, as well as the notion that the Exalted would be insufficient to handle it if they were. </div> </div> </div>Agreed. The biggest threat facing Creation is terminal, endless warfare among the Exalted, and the grinding loss of thousands of cultures and magical wonders. The Deathlords and Yozis are just flavors of the venality that drives genocidal vendettas, no more or less important than any other contributors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T08:42:36-07:00","id":1398789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398787#post1398787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. The biggest threat facing Creation is terminal, endless warfare among the Exalted, and the grinding loss of thousands of cultures and magical wonders. The Deathlords and Yozis are just flavors of the venality that drives genocidal vendettas, no more or less important than any other contributors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hopefully not <i>just</i> the Exalted - gods, elementals, ghosts, demons, sorcerers, and various mortal dictators can also take part in the cycle of violence, after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T09:42:20-07:00","id":1398806,"title":"","content":"Non-Exalted can have little an endless warfare, as a treat","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T10:25:02-07:00","id":1398819,"title":"","content":"I think it's fair to say that the Solars are the best tool available in Creation for fighting Abyssals and Infernals. If you're going up against an Abyssal or an Infernel, and you can seek the aid of a Solar, it's probably a good idea. (Especially a combat-focused Solar, but even the noncombat ones can contribute.) When, a hundred years from now, Creation is not destroyed, and not dominated by Abyssals and Deathlords, nor by Infernals and Yozis, the fact that Solars fought against them will likely be a big part of the reason why.<br /> <br /> But it's not fair to say that Solars are necessary to fight Abyssals and Infernals, no longer how big an army or whatever other support they might have. (In particular, it's not necessary if you have an even bigger army.) It's not fair to say that Creation is doomed if the Solars do not fight the Abyssals and Infernals for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> I think a good analogy might be a modern fighter aircraft. A modern fighter aircraft is the best tool available for destroying a modern fighter. If you're going up against an enemy that has a modern jet fighter, you would really like to have a fighter of your own, especially so if they have the army and everything else to back it up. But you can defeat a modern fighter with a less-advanced fighter, especially with some advantage like numbers, pilot experience, or surprise. You can defeat one, in certain situations, with anti-aircraft guns, or by destroying it on the ground, or by running away from it and waiting for the infrastructure that supports it to fall apart. You're never without hope.<br /> <br /> Exalted is a game about the Solars. But it's also a game about heroism, and never being without hope, not matter how dire the situation seems. The fact that Solars exemplify heroism does not mean that Dragonblooded and even mortals lack it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T11:44:05-07:00","id":1398832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398819#post1398819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's fair to say that the Solars are the best tool available in Creation for fighting Abyssals and Infernals. If you're going up against an Abyssal or an Infernel, and you can seek the aid of a Solar, it's probably a good idea. (Especially a combat-focused Solar, but even the noncombat ones can contribute.) When, a hundred years from now, Creation is not destroyed, and not dominated by Abyssals and Deathlords, nor by Infernals and Yozis, the fact that Solars fought against them will likely be a big part of the reason why.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is again, kind of out of date based on discussions so far from devs. The Deathlords aren't nine version sof Sauron and have their schemes that while large scale aren't existential threats to Creation by default. Abyssals are dangerous, but their empires and conquests are a difference in kind, not scale, and there's not something about them inherently that needs to be stopped save folks tend to not like dying much or having Abyssals killing their family and leaving them alive to apprecaite the results due to Chivalry of Death reasons.<br /> <br /> The Yozis are for-sure-absolutely-never-getting-out is a canon assumption, and their Exalting of Infernals is more to inflict a bunch of Killomngers or Magnetos on Creation than it is to actually conquer it. Now, an Infernal can do a shitload of damage in lashing-out or trying to change the world, but it is again, not something other Exalts have to do in order to stop some outcome.<br /> <br /> Like, this entire thing is built on a premise that Abyssals and Infernals and their patrons are existentialt hrets to Creation that have to be stood up agaisnt or they will ilnvevitably win in some fashion that dooms all of Creation. I think the gist in 3e is they are instead additional, exotic, and often unpleasanst factors that exist in the world now that make it more chaotic, dangerous, and confusing for the foreseeable future. But htey aren't like, by their existance soemthing everyone has to stand up against to stop.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398819#post1398819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's not fair to say that Solars are necessary to fight Abyssals and Infernals, no longer how big an army or whatever other support they might have. (In particular, it's not necessary if you have an even bigger army.) It's not fair to say that Creation is doomed if the Solars do not fight the Abyssals and Infernals for whatever reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creation isn't doomed due to Abyssals and Infernals around anyhow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398819#post1398819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a good analogy might be a modern fighter aircraft. A modern fighter aircraft is the best tool available for destroying a modern fighter. If you're going up against an enemy that has a modern jet fighter, you would really like to have a fighter of your own, especially so if they have the army and everything else to back it up. But you can defeat a modern fighter with a less-advanced fighter, especially with some advantage like numbers, pilot experience, or surprise. You can defeat one, in certain situations, with anti-aircraft guns, or by destroying it on the ground, or by running away from it and waiting for the infrastructure that supports it to fall apart. You're never without hope.<br /> <br /> Exalted is a game about the Solars. But it's also a game about heroism, and never being without hope, not matter how dire the situation seems. The fact that Solars exemplify heroism does not mean that Dragonblooded and even mortals lack it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a game about the Exalted. And part of that is not just deisgnating an Exalt as ahving narrative priority to a point the game caters to them exclusively, nor to have Exalts who are presented simply as purely Antagonsit Factors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T12:44:45-07:00","id":1398850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398649#post1398649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm open to suggestions for who you think can beat the godlike beings about to destroy reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the Sidereals and Dragonblooded killed all the Solars and drove the Lunars to the borders of Creation once, it's one of the biggest and most integral parts of the whole setting.<br /> <br /> Plus as others have said most of the Creation ending threats have been toned back. The Mask of Winters can <i>certainly</i> be a global threat if you want, but by default he isn't. He's a major player and a threat to the Confederation of Rivers, but he's not poised to sweep all of Creation. Which is just a way easier way of doing things for the Storyteller. I don't have to come up with 49 different explanations for why the world didn't end when the PCs have only taken care of the 50th way.<br /> <br /> Or, indeed, not even have the main plot of the story be about the destruction of the whole world at all. I can actually have a campaign that focuses around the liberation and rebuilding of a Realm satrapy.<br /> <br /> I can still very easily tune things up to be world ending threats though. It's just if I want the Reclamation to happen and a plot to release the Yozi from Hell onto Creation exists, that's one change I have to make, not dozens. Maybe I even want to come up with my own thing, where another world, like Creation, is floating through the Wyld and just now a bridge is forming between the two worlds, and what will happen then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T13:02:21-07:00","id":1398856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398787#post1398787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. The biggest threat facing Creation is terminal, endless warfare among the Exalted, and the grinding loss of thousands of cultures and magical wonders. The Deathlords and Yozis are just flavors of the venality that drives genocidal vendettas, no more or less important than any other contributors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I feel that there's an axiomatic difference between Dragonblooded Dynasts who want to rule the world, Solars who want to be BIG EPIC HEROES and genodical annihilists.<br /> <br /> Even if the Exalted didn't exist, the world would still be screwed over because there's the Fair Folk, venal asshole gods, Yozis, malevolent ghosts, Neverborn, and the fact humans are pretty scummy by themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Yozis are for-sure-absolutely-never-getting-out is a canon assumption, and their Exalting of Infernals is more to inflict a bunch of Killomngers or Magnetos on Creation than it is to actually conquer it. Now, an Infernal can do a shitload of damage in lashing-out or trying to change the world, but it is again, not something other Exalts have to do in order to stop some outcome. </div> </div> </div>Eh, the Neverborn don't want out. If they wanted out or to be reincarnated, it'd probably be healthier for reality. Instead, they have the reverse of the Yozi plan of bringing the Mountain to Muhammed by putting it all in their giant tomb.<br /> <br /> The Yozis want out since they're all in another one of their kind's stomach ala Zeus' siblings in Kronos' stomach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-25-2020, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T13:10:56-07:00","id":1398859,"title":"","content":"The Exalted already beat most of those threats once, and the ones they haven\u2019t beaten are themselves former Exalted. The only way any of them can meaningfully threaten Creation is if the Exalted weaken each other too much to sustain human civilization. Exalted violence has been the solution to so many problems that it is now Creation\u2019s biggest problem.<br /> <br /> (Don\u2019t get me wrong: those threats are real. But they all represent failure states of Exalted governance and cooperation.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T15:06:11-07:00","id":1398882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398832#post1398832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is again, kind of out of date based on discussions so far from devs. The Deathlords aren't nine version sof Sauron and have their schemes that while large scale aren't existential threats to Creation by default. Abyssals are dangerous, but their empires and conquests are a difference in kind, not scale, and there's not something about them inherently that needs to be stopped save folks tend to not like dying much or having Abyssals killing their family and leaving them alive to apprecaite the results due to Chivalry of Death reasons.<br /> <br /> The Yozis are for-sure-absolutely-never-getting-out is a canon assumption, and their Exalting of Infernals is more to inflict a bunch of Killomngers or Magnetos on Creation than it is to actually conquer it. Now, an Infernal can do a shitload of damage in lashing-out or trying to change the world, but it is again, not something other Exalts have to do in order to stop some outcome.<br /> <br /> Like, this entire thing is built on a premise that Abyssals and Infernals and their patrons are existentialt hrets to Creation that have to be stood up agaisnt or they will ilnvevitably win in some fashion that dooms all of Creation. I think the gist in 3e is they are instead additional, exotic, and often unpleasanst factors that exist in the world now that make it more chaotic, dangerous, and confusing for the foreseeable future. But htey aren't like, by their existance soemthing everyone has to stand up against to stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're interpreting what I say as a particular point of view, which I was not trying to convey. Let me explain with a different, even worse, analogy.<br /> <br /> Jeff Bezos is (probably) an ordinary, human, mortal man. I don't think he's a particularly evil man, although some people do. On the whole his influence has probably been beneficial to the world so far.<br /> <br /> But if, from now on, nobody ever stands up to or defeats Jeff Bezos, the world is going to become a very bad place. If nobody ever defeats Jeff Bezos in business competition, or using political and legal methods, or however, Amazon will gradually grow to take up a larger and larger percentage of the economy and will eventually use its market power to raise prices and funnel huge amounts of cash to itself, causing various negative consequences.<br /> <br /> You personally don't have to stop Jeff Bezos to prevent this. But someone, somewhere, has to decide they're going to go up against Jeff Bezos, do it, and win.<br /> <br /> Still, it would be ridiculous to describe him as an existential threat. He's just a businessman trying to make more money, and then use that money to make even more money.<br /> <br /> I feel like a lot of Abyssals (and a lot of Infernals, and a lot of Solars, and a lot of Dragonbloodeds, and a lot of mortals) are more dangerous for their particular region of Creation than Jeff Bezos is for Earth. They're currently building up power, and probably hurting people when they do that. If none of those people dare oppose them, they will build up more power, and end up hurting more people. If no one ever stops them, they will build up quite a lot of power, and cause quite a lot of damage. From their point of view, they probably prevented more damage than they caused. Are they right? Probably not.<br /> <br /> If nobody ever defeats any Abyssal at anything, Creation will not necessarily be drawn entirely into the Void, but there will be a lot more death and a lot of shadowlands and a lot of undead. If no one ever defeat any Infernal at anything, I don't know what will happen, but it will presumably be very, very strange and not particularly pleasant for most. (What were Magneto's and Killmonger's plans in their movies?)<br /> <br /> If you do want to defeat an Abyssal or Infernal at anything - a battle, a business competition, a philosophical discussion, a card game - it would be very convenient to have a Solar on your team. It's never necessary, but it pretty much always helps. <br /> <br /> If someone writes a history of the Time of Tumult a hundred years from now, and they don't follow the Immaculate Philosophy or something similar, there will probably be a lot of entries where an Abyssal or Infernal was trying to do something very bad, and a Solar stopped them. (There will also be a lot of entries of Solars trying to do a bad thing and getting stopped by other Exalts, unless the person writing it works for the Gold Faction. It's all in the game.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Creation isn't doomed due to Abyssals and Infernals around anyhow. </div> </div> </div>That's fair.<br /> <br /> My understanding is that the devs didn't intend to communicate any particular stance on whether there are existential threats to Creation. You can have your group of PCs fight a plot to destroy Creation by a Deathlord if you want. You can have them spend the entire game arguing about philosophy and religion if you want.<br /> <br /> For me it makes sense to say that there are a lot of existential threats to Creation, or at least a lot of threats to large chunks of Creation, but that other Exalts, and sometimes even mortals, are constantly stopping them, which the PCs don't necessarily even hear about. Creation is doomed in the sense that if no one stopped any of the Deathlords, Fair Folk, unbound second circle demons, unruly gods, ambitious Dragonblooded generals, etc., etc., etc. that threaten it, most human civilization would be destroyed. But that actually happening is about as likely as all those threats being simultaneously stopped and everyone living in harmony forevermore, because brave, heroic individuals exist - for example, the PCs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a game about the Exalted. And part of that is not just deisgnating an Exalt as ahving narrative priority to a point the game caters to them exclusively, nor to have Exalts who are presented simply as purely Antagonsit Factors. </div> </div> </div>This is 100% true. But it's an intentional part of the game design that Solars, Abyssals, and Infernals have the greatest potential for strength, and ease of reaching that potential, in a one-on-one, fair, fight. A portion of the narrative for the other Exalts is about finding ways to not get into a one-on-one, fair fight.<br /> <br /> It's also an intentional part of the game design that some Exalt types are more likely to be an antagonist, and some more likely to be a protagonist. <br /> <br /> The Solars can be special, and the PC's Solars can be especially special, and they can be the only ones to save Creation from some great evil, without the 150 living Solars collectively drinking up all the protagonist juice and all being absolutely essential to facing any of 150 existential threats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T18:16:27-07:00","id":1398912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398859#post1398859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exalted already beat most of those threats once, and the ones they haven\u2019t beaten are themselves former Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm of two minds. On the one is where it speaks a lot to why I don't much care for a focus on existential threats at all. I think the setting is most interesting when it's complex and multifaceted and various actors have various levels of dispute with one another. I dislike too much of a framing of that in terms of the big threat that stands right outside their door ready to punish them for their lack of uniformity or impose an inorganic impetus for unification.<br /> <br /> On the other, a hypothetical narrative of the Balorian Crusade facing off against something like a largely united Exalted Host is one that I would hope would play out in a more dramatic and engaging manner than &quot;the Exalted inevitably win&quot;. On this count, I think the developers might disagree with some of your premise when they've referred to the Primordial War as having not been a sure thing.<br /> <br /> I like the power of the Exalted, but I find that some of the latter sentiment leans in a direction of presuming that power includes the form of endless emotional reserves or only ever making the best decisions, which to me is just a bit...<br /> <br /> Kimochi warui.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T18:49:46-07:00","id":1398916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398882#post1398882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're interpreting what I say as a particular point of view, which I was not trying to convey. Let me explain with a different, even worse, analogy.<br /> <br /> Jeff Bezos is (probably) an ordinary, human, mortal man. I don't think he's a particularly evil man, although some people do. On the whole his influence has probably been beneficial to the world so far.<br /> <br /> But if, from now on, nobody ever stands up to or defeats Jeff Bezos, the world is going to become a very bad place. If nobody ever defeats Jeff Bezos in business competition, or using political and legal methods, or however, Amazon will gradually grow to take up a larger and larger percentage of the economy and will eventually use its market power to raise prices and funnel huge amounts of cash to itself, causing various negative consequences.<br /> <br /> You personally don't have to stop Jeff Bezos to prevent this. But someone, somewhere, has to decide they're going to go up against Jeff Bezos, do it, and win.<br /> <br /> Still, it would be ridiculous to describe him as an existential threat. He's just a businessman trying to make more money, and then use that money to make even more money.</div> </div> </div> </div>The existential threats are the businessmen who make their &quot;more money&quot; by burning fossil fuels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T19:40:13-07:00","id":1398924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398912#post1398912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other, a hypothetical narrative of the Balorian Crusade facing off against something like a largely united Exalted Host is one that I would hope would play out in a more dramatic and engaging manner than &quot;the Exalted inevitably win&quot;. On this count, I think the developers might disagree with some of your premise when they've referred to the Primordial War as having not been a sure thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>They might! I don't speak for them, for the record.<br /> <br /> That said, I agree with you that it's not impossible for an external threat to arise that could challenge or overwhelm the might of the combined Exalted Host. I simply think that the Time of Tumult is named such because it comes down to how the Exalted quarrel over and manage the world they've built. Second Edition's Thousand Dooms were a movement away from the political and toward the power fantasy. But my observation so far has been that Third Edition has conspicuously avoided presenting any Ozymandias-esque glaringly-obvious problems designed to get the Exalted to put aside their differences. Those threats can arise at your table, but they aren't the focus of what we've been writing about, because truly apocalyptic dooms make all the challenging personal and political stuff--which is the bread-and-butter of <i>Exalted</i>--feel petty, or at least safely ignorable.<br /> <br /> And any of the problems we've already mentioned <i>can become</i> apocalyptic problems if the Exalted truly, truly screw up. The Exalted aren't invulnerable, but they've ruled Creation for millennia, and the most likely (and most thematically interesting) problems Creation might face are a result of that history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T19:46:43-07:00","id":1398926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398882#post1398882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think [Jeff Bezos is] a particularly evil man, although some people do. On the whole his influence has probably been beneficial to the world so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like onions and ogres, Jeff Bezos has layers. <br /> <br /> One layer has him stealing his Amazon Whole Foods\u2019 employees\u2019 healthcare and building another mansion for himself, less than a year before a massive pandemic hit the world.<br /> <br /> Another layer has him working his employees to death to fund a stupid space rocket so he can escape the consequences of his actions.<br /> <br /> How much do you need to peel this onion before you realize that the whole thing is rotten?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398882#post1398882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If nobody ever defeats Jeff Bezos in business competition, or using political and legal methods, or however, Amazon will gradually grow to take up a larger and larger percentage of the economy and will eventually use its market power to raise prices and funnel huge amounts of cash to itself, causing various negative consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>The scary thing is, if someone beats Jeff Bezos in business, they\u2019ll almost certainly have done it by becoming the next Jeff Bezos.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"https://www.cracked.com/article_27944_4-underreported-ways-amazon-makes-world-worse.html\" target=\"_blank\">Relevant article.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-27-2020, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T19:56:37-07:00","id":1398931,"title":"","content":"As ever, it also occurs to me that a significant shortcoming to the perspective of &quot;if the Solars don't prevent the Abyssals and Infernals from destroying the world, then who will&quot; is that it cultivates an attitude that precludes an answer of... &quot;Each other&quot;.<br /> <br /> By which I do not mean &quot;the bad guys run on the typical authoritarian playbook of continuously undermining their own agenda by the endemic distrust, pettiness, spite and ambition that are the hallmarks of their villainy&quot;, but rather a lack of regard for the possibility of them having wildly different agendas from one another.<br /> <br /> Not to mention the compelling image of an Abyssal or Infernal rising to power in a manner much the same as a Solar would, except where a lot of the key motifs differ. We never got much about Basphomy in Verdegris, but I don't exactly see the end of the world that only a Solar can avert in her story of railing against her underprivileged background by seating herself at a big table draped in velvet, covered in glitz and turning into a sonic boom dragon when she needs to remind somebody who's boss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T23:46:24-07:00","id":1398956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398926#post1398926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like onions and ogres, Jeff Bezos has layers. <br /> <br /> One layer has him stealing his Amazon Whole Foods\u2019 employees\u2019 healthcare and building another mansion for himself, less than a year before a massive pandemic hit the world.<br /> <br /> Another layer has him working his employees to death to fund a stupid space rocket so he can escape the consequences of his actions.<br /> <br /> How much do you need to peel this onion before you realize that the whole thing is rotten?<br /> <br /> The scary thing is, if someone beats Jeff Bezos in business, they\u2019ll almost certainly have done it by becoming the next Jeff Bezos.</div> </div> </div> </div>And another layer has a $15 minimum wage for Amazon employees, providing goods for the poorest in society at the lowest prices, and offering an international service that millions of people want. To say nothing of pushing the boundaries of science and...<br /> <br /> Can we debate Jeff Bezos in Offtopic or something? And by &quot;we&quot; I mean &quot;I really don't want to debate Jeff Bezos with anyone, but I especially don't want to do it on an Exalted forum&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398912#post1398912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm of two minds. On the one is where it speaks a lot to why I don't much care for a focus on existential threats at all. I think the setting is most interesting when it's complex and multifaceted and various actors have various levels of dispute with one another. I dislike too much of a framing of that in terms of the big threat that stands right outside their door ready to punish them for their lack of uniformity or impose an inorganic impetus for unification.<br /> <br /> On the other, a hypothetical narrative of the Balorian Crusade facing off against something like a largely united Exalted Host is one that I would hope would play out in a more dramatic and engaging manner than &quot;the Exalted inevitably win&quot;. On this count, I think the developers might disagree with some of your premise when they've referred to the Primordial War as having not been a sure thing.<br /> <br /> I like the power of the Exalted, but I find that some of the latter sentiment leans in a direction of presuming that power includes the form of endless emotional reserves or only ever making the best decisions, which to me is just a bit...<br /> <br /> Kimochi warui.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Exalted would &quot;invariably win&quot;.<br /> <br /> But let's not forget that what started this tangent is the assertion that the Exalted would invariably <b>lose</b> against an existential threat. Pointing out that last time the Exalted fought threat &quot;X&quot;, the Exalted kicked its ass, is pretty good evidence that they're not hopelessly doomed if a Second Balor were to rise.<br /> <br /> Maybe they'll win. Maybe they won't. Roll Initiative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T00:13:54-07:00","id":1398957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398956#post1398956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we debate Jeff Bezos in Offtopic or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d really rather not treat this like a debate at all; if you are conscious of all the evil he\u2019s done, and still advocate for him, then we\u2019re <i>never</i> going to see eye to eye. I\u2019m not interested in what any one man has to offer, if he has to offer it to me from atop a pyramid of skulls.<br /> <br /> That said, you\u2019re right that this is off-topic.<br /> <br /> So back to the subject at hand. I agree that the Exalted punch above their weight class, so they don\u2019t <i>necessarily</i> need to all unify to <i>potentially</i> stop some existential outside threat\u2026 but I\u2019d still just as soon not see some existential outside threat presented to us in the gameline, and am grateful that the developers seem to agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-26-2020, 05:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T02:58:54-07:00","id":1398988,"title":"","content":"Incoming ramble basically repeating my now standardized thoughts when this topic of apocalyptic threats comes about : <br /> <br /> My feeling on apocalyptic threats is; presenting them as an inevitable consequence of the inertia of the world should the Solars not intervene, flattens out the trajectory of where stories go in Exalted and flattens out the dialogue between Exalted factions about who should rule and how they should interact. <br /> <br /> It's absolutely fine and fun for individual games to introduce &quot;Apocalyptic Battle of Darkness Against The Light&quot; type of scenarios, but seems to me better for everything around the setting generally if these are million-to-one events that just happen to have happened in a given game (and will do in waaay more than one in a million games!), due to outside MacGuffinry. Not an inevitable outgrowth of its fundamental internal historical forces and its design.<br /> <br /> Exalted's really well set up as a fantasy game for &quot;Epic fantasy where the fate of nations and kingdoms lies in the balance!&quot; (whether the sort that places agency with general and kings, or the sort that places agency with a small and plucky band of journeying heroes) and it's a shame to compress that towards &quot;Epic Fantasy Against the Dark Lord, Lest The World Be Destroyed!&quot; scenarios where it's &quot;Solars or Bust!&quot;.<br /> <br /> (This is roughly similar to some other takes by writers / devs in the past, I think?)<br /> <br /> (As a further caveat, I totally get and have some sympathy to the objection to this that lots of fans bought into a vision of Exalted where Solars with &quot;cosmic power&quot; -power they alone have among the Exalted - fought against &quot;cosmic threats&quot; to preserve reality from destruction. That sounds fun! But at the end of the day I don't think this has priority of claim, or is making the best use of the way the world is set up!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T03:07:26-07:00","id":1398990,"title":"","content":"My Sunday game\u2019s gone for over a year now without a cosmic threat, thankfully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T06:26:11-07:00","id":1399047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398926#post1398926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like onions and ogres, Jeff Bezos has layers.<br /> <br /> One layer has him stealing his Amazon Whole Foods\u2019 employees\u2019 healthcare and building another mansion for himself, less than a year before a massive pandemic hit the world.<br /> <br /> Another layer has him working his employees to death to fund a stupid space rocket so he can escape the consequences of his actions.<br /> <br /> How much do you need to peel this onion before you realize that the whole thing is rotten?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point and I guess I didn't pick a very good example. I would discuss more, but, as you mentioned later, this is off-topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The scary thing is, if someone beats Jeff Bezos in business, they\u2019ll almost certainly have done it by becoming the next Jeff Bezos. </div> </div> </div>The implications of this for Exalted are fairly obvious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398392-is-usurpation-the-right-term-still-in-3e?p=1398990#post1398990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Sunday game\u2019s gone for over a year now without a cosmic threat, thankfully.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! We haven't had any threat larger than one city-state, although I guess we're aware that the Mask of Winters probably has some larger designs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","user":"habitableexoplanet","date":". 06-26-2020, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}